WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:07.939
In 1997, a massive, gray cloud of gas and
smog settled over the ordinary town of Daleport,

00:00:07.939 --> 00:00:09.019
New England.

00:00:09.019 --> 00:00:13.599
Phone lines were cut off, and any attempts
to enter the town were met with failure.

00:00:13.599 --> 00:00:20.300
There was a complete and total blackout of
information coming in and out of Daleport.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:25.400
Whatever was occurring it was anything but
normal, and clashed with the town’s easygoing

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:26.869
and peaceful atmosphere.

00:00:26.869 --> 00:00:32.340
An anomalous event of this size and scale
was impossible to miss, and naturally caught

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:37.110
the attention of the SCP Foundation before
it did the outside media, who would report

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:41.570
on the mysterious occurrence and draw unnecessary
amounts of attention to the town.

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:46.040
The Foundation was lucky enough to maintain
a hold over the situation little over 3 hours

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:51.730
after it had begun, and they already started
their usual cover-up story operations, keeping

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:55.040
the situation in Daleport well away from the
public eye.

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:59.700
Still, they were unsure of what was occurring,
and what they were dealing with themselves.

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:04.670
If they were going to get to the bottom of
this mysterious smog covering an average New

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:09.620
England town, they were going to be safe,
and have to play it resourcefully, as the

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:12.540
SCP Foundation is known for doing.

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:18.550
The status of Daleport’s residents, whether
they were alive or dead, was completely unknown,

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:21.280
and so the Foundation began their rescue efforts.

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:26.070
A containment perimeter surrounding the town
was established, and relevant witnesses outside

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:31.060
of the town were detained and amnesticized,
with convincing cover-stories already being

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:32.060
deployed.

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:37.200
For the Foundation, even an entire town undergoing
an anomalous event was something they were

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:42.060
well-prepared to deal with, having handled
similar situations multiple times over the

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:43.210
decades.

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:48.500
The Foundation began its research on Daleport
by observing what exactly the cloud of smog

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:50.370
covering the town was.

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:55.729
The Foundation wasn’t keen on sending its
personnel, even the so-called disposable D-Class,

00:01:55.729 --> 00:02:01.180
to their death, so the first exploration into
the cloud was carried out by an unmanned ground

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:05.229
vehicle operating under the callsign ‘UGV-1’.

00:02:05.229 --> 00:02:10.940
This unstoppable carrier was equipped with
all the stops, including atmospheric sampling

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:16.730
sensors, audio-video recording equipment,
and a open-circuit biological sampling instrument,

00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:21.670
which contained skin tissue and several live
brown rats, whose reactions would indicate

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:26.610
to the Foundation whether or not the smog
was safe to be exposed to or not.

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:31.020
The ground vehicle departed, and when it returned
about a half hour later, it brought with it

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:34.670
a whole host of data about the gas covering
Daleport.

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:40.900
As it turned out, the smog was composed of
sulfer, nitrogen, and carbon oxides concentrated

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:46.640
at a level where irritation would occur upon
contact with humans but it wasn’t lethal.

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:51.780
Neither was it anomalous, as the samples the
vehicle carried in with it were unaffected

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:53.730
in any anomalous manner.

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:58.770
The video recording displayed a flat, empty
wasteland inside the gas cluster, with little

00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:00.790
discernible features.

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:05.170
After a certain point, radio communication
with the vehicle became degraded, and the

00:03:05.170 --> 00:03:08.480
Foundation returned the carrier to the town’s
perimeter.

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:13.410
As more resources and supplies arrived on
location, the Foundation ramped up its research

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:14.440
efforts.

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:20.080
This time, two D-Class were sent into the
gas cluster, both aboard another ground vehicle

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:21.080
carrier.

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:24.430
This time, the truck was equipped with a higher
wattage radio transceiver than that of the

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:28.620
first one, which the Foundation hoped would
be enough to maintain communication throughout

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:29.620
the anomaly.

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:34.580
At a kilometer from the boundary, the D-Class
unboarded the vehicle and were asked to remove

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:36.000
their protective suits.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:40.880
They experienced no anomalous effects from
exposure to the gas, but medical telemetry

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:44.300
showed that one of the D-class was having
difficulty breathing.

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:48.980
The duo reported the same flat, featureless
terrain the first vehicle’s recording had

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:49.980
captured.

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:53.660
When radio interference occurred again, the
Foundation pulled the vehicle back, and the

00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:58.760
two D-Class were recovered safely, with no
abnormal effects occurring as a result of

00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:00.569
being exposed to the gas.

00:04:00.569 --> 00:04:04.990
Still, there was no indication of what was
actually occurring in Daleport.

00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:10.030
It was only that lifeless, gray horizon, and
the Foundation wanted answers.

00:04:10.030 --> 00:04:15.080
A third expedition was carried out, this time
manned by Mobile Task Force operatives equipped

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:19.059
with all of the latest gear, as well as several
large vehicles.

00:04:19.059 --> 00:04:23.629
The vehicles split up, but communications
quickly pointed out differences between the

00:04:23.629 --> 00:04:25.009
team’s surroundings.

00:04:25.009 --> 00:04:30.039
One spotted an upward incline, while the others
only saw the same terrain as before.

00:04:30.039 --> 00:04:34.419
Minutes later, the incline team reported that
they were going down an incline.

00:04:34.419 --> 00:04:37.939
The team that hadn’t seen the incline reported
that they were now seeing it, and that they

00:04:37.939 --> 00:04:40.550
were following the other vehicle downwards.

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:45.069
Another team noticed red and blue patterns
in the sky, while voices on the radios began

00:04:45.069 --> 00:04:47.999
speaking in an unknown language.

00:04:47.999 --> 00:04:53.230
After minutes of radio interference, the Foundation
picked up the sound of a firefight, with mobile

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:58.220
task force operatives giving wildly varying
descriptions of the attacking forces.

00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:03.490
Whatever was happening was incomprehensible,
and for whatever reason, the Foundation was

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:07.110
entirely unable to communicate through their
radios.

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:11.759
After around 30 minutes of noise, an unknown
voice gave a mysterious, gibberish-filled

00:05:11.759 --> 00:05:13.180
message to the Foundation.

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:19.129
It’s a little silly to hear, but there’s
certainly some strange undertones within.

00:05:19.129 --> 00:05:25.990
The voice said:
“Blargh, I am Ssvlsrr, the Shivering Mist.

00:05:25.990 --> 00:05:34.499
I am the n'ghft currently covering the town
of Daleport.

00:05:34.499 --> 00:05:43.270
While traversing my ftaghu, your men have
been attacked.

00:05:43.270 --> 00:05:50.279
Some have become n'gha, but the rest are in
safe hands.

00:05:50.279 --> 00:05:58.259
Evil has been summoned to this town, by a
society of hlirghh.

00:05:58.259 --> 00:06:04.440
The worst shall be contained within me by
vulgtmm and tharanakk, but the town and its

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:10.449
people will not remain unaffected.

00:06:10.449 --> 00:06:17.240
A great battle shall rage and a victor must
be decided.

00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:26.509
In time, those who can stop the ehye will
be here in time and see the hlirghh fm'latgh.

00:06:26.509 --> 00:06:37.349
Please do not send any more soldiers into
me as I cannot keep them from the shogg.

00:06:37.349 --> 00:06:48.520
When all throd before the victors, I shall
leave and the shugg will be yours again.

00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:55.370
I hope you shall survive it.

00:06:55.370 --> 00:06:56.539
Y'hah.”

00:06:56.539 --> 00:07:01.199
It was clear that something had taken over
the town of Daleport, and that this mysterious

00:07:01.199 --> 00:07:06.080
voice, while threatening sounding, was apparently
protecting the people inside.

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:11.610
It mentioned that the Foundation’s men were
in safe hands, and that evil had been summoned

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:12.819
to the town.

00:07:12.819 --> 00:07:16.589
The Foundation didn’t know what to make
of the message, or if they could trust the

00:07:16.589 --> 00:07:18.000
entity that made it.

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:20.240
But they didn’t have much of a choice.

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:24.830
They attempted to send more unmanned operations
into the town, but they were unable to reach

00:07:24.830 --> 00:07:30.479
their destination, somehow always winding
up back where they started shortly after departing.

00:07:30.479 --> 00:07:35.089
After a week and a half of fruitless expeditions
and no new information, the gas blocking the

00:07:35.089 --> 00:07:40.520
town of Daleport dissipated completely, leaving
the town accessible and able to be explored

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:42.520
fully by the Foundation.

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:47.499
A containment crew fully set-up a perimeter
around the area, with secure cameras and an

00:07:47.499 --> 00:07:53.199
entire facility on the outskirts of Daleport,
named Area-37, to oversee and support the

00:07:53.199 --> 00:08:01.259
Foundation’s research inside the town, which
was now officially categorized as SCP-1936.

00:08:01.259 --> 00:08:05.409
With the gas now dissipated, the Foundation
began to investigate the anomalous effects

00:08:05.409 --> 00:08:06.860
left in its wake.

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:12.410
The town itself was altered, with buildings
physically differing from their previous states,

00:08:12.410 --> 00:08:16.179
and a large portion of them having become
topologically inconsistent.

00:08:16.179 --> 00:08:20.990
There were rooms that would appear bigger
or smaller than they should be, with some

00:08:20.990 --> 00:08:26.149
growing so small after they had been entered
that they trapped occupants inside and prevented

00:08:26.149 --> 00:08:30.740
them from moving, resulting in a number of
unretrievable Foundation personnel becoming

00:08:30.740 --> 00:08:33.970
stuck and lost inside the anomaly forever.

00:08:33.970 --> 00:08:38.260
Other doors would lead to different locations
at different times of the day, or corridors

00:08:38.260 --> 00:08:43.550
that led to multiple locations at the same
time despite only leading to one.

00:08:43.550 --> 00:08:48.190
These difficult to describe spatial anomalies
were so dangerous and unpredictable that the

00:08:48.190 --> 00:08:54.280
Foundation forbade any exploration into SCP-1936
without explicit authorization.

00:08:54.280 --> 00:08:58.560
But while the town itself was affected, what
about the people inside it?

00:08:58.560 --> 00:09:03.250
The normal people who were caught up in the
anomalous fate of Daleport, what happened

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:04.250
to them?

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:08.900
The Foundation was unsure, and while no survivors
were found within the town itself, a large

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:13.820
number of human remains of Daleport citizens
were recovered during the exploration efforts.

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:18.510
Most of these remains demonstrated anomalous
properties, presumably gained as a result

00:09:18.510 --> 00:09:23.180
of the devastating anomalous disaster that
plagued the town a week prior.

00:09:23.180 --> 00:09:26.820
Some of the remains the Foundation recovered
were incredibly strange.

00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:32.370
Such as a smear of entrails found alongside
a small plant that gave out a constant flame.

00:09:32.370 --> 00:09:37.460
The pile of viscera picked up radio transmissions
from up to six miles away, with sound being

00:09:37.460 --> 00:09:40.080
created through vibration of tissues.

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:43.310
Another was a torso embedded in the wall of
a building.

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:48.430
Slight movement of the torso was visible when
investigating personnel spoke, and blood continually

00:09:48.430 --> 00:09:52.880
manifested in mid-air, fifteen centimeters
above the torso.

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:58.120
On the main street of the town, several corpses
were discovered with their flesh, skin, and

00:09:58.120 --> 00:10:01.960
bone all removed from a circular portion of
their foreheads.

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:06.920
Skin and brain tissue surrounding their wounds
had undergone severe charring.

00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:12.740
Outside of the public library, several floating
torsos manifest at a certain time each day,

00:10:12.740 --> 00:10:15.990
simulating the motions of running alongside
the road.

00:10:15.990 --> 00:10:19.160
After three minutes, the torsos attempt to
leave the road and fade out.

00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:24.190
A young woman’s body floats steadily upwards
when any force is applied to it, regardless

00:10:24.190 --> 00:10:25.800
of the force’s direction.

00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:30.620
The body is currently suspended 57 meters
above the ground, floating over Daleport.

00:10:30.620 --> 00:10:34.830
And these are just some of the strange anomalies
found within SCP-1936.

00:10:34.830 --> 00:10:40.490
While it’s unknown what happened to these
civilians, their bodies were clearly affected

00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:45.000
by whatever occured the week prior while the
Foundation was unable to access the town of

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:46.380
Daleport.

00:10:46.380 --> 00:10:51.120
Something in that strange, anomalous gas triggered
a highly destructive event that had grave

00:10:51.120 --> 00:10:55.970
consequences for ordinary people, and the
Foundation was none the wiser as to what it

00:10:55.970 --> 00:10:56.970
was.

00:10:56.970 --> 00:11:01.420
Still, they continued their search of the
area, and over the next few weeks, they discovered

00:11:01.420 --> 00:11:05.400
a number of recovered materials from the wreckage
and debris of SCP-1936.

00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:12.490
The first were a series of written documents,
composed by the town’s previous inhabitants.

00:11:12.490 --> 00:11:18.180
These were recovered from laptops and journals,
but read in that same, nonsensical tone that

00:11:18.180 --> 00:11:22.650
the mysterious voice spoke in during the Mobile
Task Force’s expedition.

00:11:22.650 --> 00:11:26.630
One note said that the writer was running
out of canned food, and that there was constant

00:11:26.630 --> 00:11:31.500
screaming coming from outside their house,
and something trying to break into it.

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:36.130
The note talked about the town’s reverend,
described as having ‘too many spaces in

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:41.160
him’ who was walking past the writer’s
windows and ranting about total nonsense.

00:11:41.160 --> 00:11:45.890
The note also read that the writer was fearing
that, as they put it, ‘one of the big guys’

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:51.700
was coming their way, and that they could
hear the pounding, constant sound of drums.

00:11:51.700 --> 00:11:58.740
But one note remains consistent, found in
multiple locations throughout SCP-1936, predominantly

00:11:58.740 --> 00:12:04.760
in public toilets and stitched into the internal
organs of the Daleport resident’s bodies.

00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:08.770
It reads “I am so sorry that I could not
save you.

00:12:08.770 --> 00:12:10.430
Signed, Pangloss.”

00:12:10.430 --> 00:12:15.360
The Foundation had heard rumblings and rumors
of the entity known as Pangloss, who was supposedly

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:20.020
a god with a helpful affinity for humanity,
but there was no concrete evidence pointing

00:12:20.020 --> 00:12:22.480
towards the being’s existence.

00:12:22.480 --> 00:12:25.990
Whatever happened in Daleport, was Pangloss
trying to stop it?

00:12:25.990 --> 00:12:28.720
The message certainly reads that way.

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:32.600
Surveillance footage from a gas station painted
an even more terrifying picture.

00:12:32.600 --> 00:12:37.320
An ordinary gas station cashier was doing
his job ringing out a customer’s items,

00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:41.790
when the window next to him smashed open,
and an impossible-looking, tentacle-filled

00:12:41.790 --> 00:12:44.280
entity made its way into the building.

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:49.000
The tentacle creature lashed out at the two
of them, brutally murdering the customer with

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:52.690
the force of the impact of its slippery, writhing
appendage.

00:12:52.690 --> 00:12:56.790
The cashier hid behind the counter, but the
footage shows the entity also making its way

00:12:56.790 --> 00:13:01.630
behind the counter, and the gruesome visual
of blood splattering the walls behind the

00:13:01.630 --> 00:13:05.330
register as the entity quickly took the cashier’s
life.

00:13:05.330 --> 00:13:10.980
But then, mysteriously, an individual enters
the gas station, wearing a bowler hat and

00:13:10.980 --> 00:13:12.020
a waistcoat.

00:13:12.020 --> 00:13:14.220
The footage distorts as they enter the shot.

00:13:14.220 --> 00:13:16.430
Then, their face is revealed.

00:13:16.430 --> 00:13:21.540
Instead of ordinary features, like a mouth
or eyes, they have a triangle branded into

00:13:21.540 --> 00:13:22.670
their skin.

00:13:22.670 --> 00:13:26.680
The tentacle entity moved back in fear of
this well-dressed individual, clearly afraid

00:13:26.680 --> 00:13:27.680
of them.

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:32.270
Then, a series of multi-jointed appendages
burst forth from various points on the individual’s

00:13:32.270 --> 00:13:36.280
body, and they lunged forward, attacking the
tentacle-entity.

00:13:36.280 --> 00:13:39.820
The footage cuts off there, with the individual
throwing the tentacle creature through the

00:13:39.820 --> 00:13:41.570
wall of the gas station.

00:13:41.570 --> 00:13:46.160
Whoever this individual was, it was clear
that they didn’t take kindly to the rampaging

00:13:46.160 --> 00:13:47.910
tentacle entity.

00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:53.000
Some Foundation researchers began to speculate
that the individual was Pangloss themselves,

00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:56.800
who was trying to save Daleport as best as
they could, but there was obviously no way

00:13:56.800 --> 00:14:00.320
to be certain of the mysterious person’s
identity.

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:05.250
More footage showed a car crash outside of
a public library, which resulted in a spectral,

00:14:05.250 --> 00:14:09.570
translucent entity breaking free from the
broken lamppost that the vehicle collided

00:14:09.570 --> 00:14:10.570
into.

00:14:10.570 --> 00:14:15.100
The car’s passengers immediately ran, but
the ghost-like entity chased after them.

00:14:15.100 --> 00:14:20.040
This continues until the ghost emits a large,
blue shockwave of unknown energy, which passes

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:25.440
over the people, turning them completely transparent,
and causing them to fade away.

00:14:25.440 --> 00:14:30.010
The Foundation recognized that it was another
mysterious, surreal entity rampaging through

00:14:30.010 --> 00:14:31.010
Daleport.

00:14:31.010 --> 00:14:35.010
Clearly, whatever happened here was anything
but normal.

00:14:35.010 --> 00:14:39.360
Another collection of footage, this time focusing
around Daleport’s town hall, depicted the

00:14:39.360 --> 00:14:41.210
building in complete ruin.

00:14:41.210 --> 00:14:46.590
The roof was collapsed, the front doors were
missing, and the entire structure was toned

00:14:46.590 --> 00:14:48.590
in a blue-violet hue.

00:14:48.590 --> 00:14:54.300
In front of the building was a convoy of vehicles,
civilian trucks and cars, as well as the ground

00:14:54.300 --> 00:14:59.350
vehicles of the Mobile Task Force squads that
went missing after they were sent into the

00:14:59.350 --> 00:15:00.350
anomaly.

00:15:00.350 --> 00:15:03.820
It was clear this footage took place shortly
after the Foundation attempted to enter the

00:15:03.820 --> 00:15:08.600
gas surrounding Daleport, and lost connection
with the task forces that were sent in.

00:15:08.600 --> 00:15:13.000
The footage shows the Foundation soldiers
as well as the civilians of the town fighting

00:15:13.000 --> 00:15:18.010
against another strange looking entity, this
time shaped like a fractal structure.

00:15:18.010 --> 00:15:22.560
Eventually, they retreat into the town hall
building, narrowly escaping from the strange

00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:27.100
creature and directly into a circular blue-violet
vortex.

00:15:27.100 --> 00:15:31.640
After all of the civilians and personnel have
escaped, the phrase ‘PANGLOSS GRANTS YOU

00:15:31.640 --> 00:15:35.830
SANCTUARY’ is burned into the stonework
above the town hall’s entrance.

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:40.980
It was this footage that gave the Foundation
a better idea of what occurred in SCP-1936,

00:15:40.980 --> 00:15:45.029
though the strangeness of the visuals didn’t
clear much up.

00:15:45.029 --> 00:15:50.110
Whatever disaster happened in Daleport, whatever
resulted in these absurd, hostile entities

00:15:50.110 --> 00:15:55.660
being unleashed upon the town, was actively
combated by Pangloss, the deity who was trying

00:15:55.660 --> 00:15:58.000
its best to move civilians to safety.

00:15:58.000 --> 00:15:59.920
But one question remained.

00:15:59.920 --> 00:16:04.190
If Pangloss was transporting civilians to
safety, where did they wind up?

00:16:04.190 --> 00:16:07.740
Why did the Foundation not discover any survivors
inside Daleport?

00:16:07.740 --> 00:16:13.410
Well, their answer came a few weeks later,
when in a shocking turn of events, 94 live

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:19.560
civilians and nearly all of the missing Foundation
personnel manifested inside the Area-37 facility.

00:16:19.560 --> 00:16:24.410
Pangloss’s emergency escape method worked,
and the civilians were confirmed alive and

00:16:24.410 --> 00:16:25.410
without harm.

00:16:25.410 --> 00:16:29.130
It’s not very often that missing persons
are actually recovered in the Foundation’s

00:16:29.130 --> 00:16:34.490
line of work, so hats off to Pangloss for
managing to do some good in this horrifying

00:16:34.490 --> 00:16:35.490
situation.

00:16:35.490 --> 00:16:39.120
Interviews with the recovered individuals
indicated that they all suffered memory loss

00:16:39.120 --> 00:16:43.740
regarding the events of Daleport, so unfortunately,
there was no new information to be gained

00:16:43.740 --> 00:16:45.089
from their recovery.

00:16:45.089 --> 00:16:50.320
But inside the anomaly, Foundation expedition
teams uncovered more documents and pieces

00:16:50.320 --> 00:16:56.250
of evidence, this time referring to a cult
named the Victory Society, which the Foundation

00:16:56.250 --> 00:17:01.920
began to believe were the cause of the mysterious
gas arriving over Daleport, and the town’s

00:17:01.920 --> 00:17:02.920
destruction.

00:17:02.920 --> 00:17:07.389
Little is known about the Victory Society,
but it is believed to be a religious organization

00:17:07.389 --> 00:17:09.639
that was localized to Daleport.

00:17:09.639 --> 00:17:13.939
One note, recovered from the body of a Victory
Society member, was a list of things that

00:17:13.939 --> 00:17:19.059
the cult needed, which included a strange
and ridiculous combination of items, including

00:17:19.059 --> 00:17:25.139
two trout, a bottle of milk, beetles, ice,
dead bodies, human eyes, and assorted souls.

00:17:25.139 --> 00:17:29.720
In the margins of the note, there were more
personal thoughts, which the writer lamented

00:17:29.720 --> 00:17:32.799
the difficulty in acquiring some of the objects.

00:17:32.799 --> 00:17:36.910
Another note was found on the inside of a
book, this time detailing a great religious

00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:41.160
battle between gods and entities that the
Foundation had never heard of.

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:46.029
Once again, it was written in that lofty,
nonsensical tone, detailing an all-encompassing

00:17:46.029 --> 00:17:50.740
mist that would descend upon the world, which
would prevent those from entering the location

00:17:50.740 --> 00:17:56.150
the text described as the place where an event
known as the ‘awakening’ would occur.

00:17:56.150 --> 00:18:00.799
If this text was to be believed, Daleport
was the center of a battle between incredibly

00:18:00.799 --> 00:18:05.869
powerful extra-dimensional anomalous entities,
who clashed together with little regard for

00:18:05.869 --> 00:18:07.159
the residents of the town.

00:18:07.159 --> 00:18:12.340
It seemed that Pangloss, the entity who saved
the civilians, was just trying their best

00:18:12.340 --> 00:18:17.440
to move as many people as they could to safety,
away from the havoc of the surreal battleground

00:18:17.440 --> 00:18:19.399
that Daleport was becoming.

00:18:19.399 --> 00:18:23.580
More documents, this time from the Victory
Society’s Reverend leader, detailed the

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:25.700
cult performing a ritual.

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:30.379
Again and again, the reverend stated in his
notes that the ritual was for, in his words,

00:18:30.379 --> 00:18:35.019
“The good of everybody”, and that “the
victor” would “walk from the rubbles of

00:18:35.019 --> 00:18:38.240
man and restore clarity to those who remain.”

00:18:38.240 --> 00:18:42.570
The notes also included a transcription of
a speech given by the reverand, in which he

00:18:42.570 --> 00:18:46.809
addressed the Victory Society cult with haunting
premonitions of what was to come.

00:18:46.809 --> 00:18:49.110
His voice painted a harrowing picture:

00:18:49.110 --> 00:18:54.360
“Brothers and sisters, we come together
to bid farewell today.

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:57.200
It has been an honor to work with you all.

00:18:57.200 --> 00:19:03.570
I could not have hoped for a better group
with which to secure the future of mankind.

00:19:03.570 --> 00:19:09.070
From the dawn of time, terrible impossibilities
have spawned from the darkness between stars,

00:19:09.070 --> 00:19:13.600
not hating life, simply being indifferent
to it.

00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:18.850
We are as ants to these abominations, these
demented Gods.

00:19:18.850 --> 00:19:23.360
They are so far above us that we are but insects.

00:19:23.360 --> 00:19:26.340
Accordingly, we shall look as such.

00:19:26.340 --> 00:19:31.749
In order to gain the forgiveness and favor
of the Gods, we must learn to know our place

00:19:31.749 --> 00:19:32.749
before them.

00:19:32.749 --> 00:19:39.179
Each of these things seeks dominion over the
laws of reality itself, imposing the nature

00:19:39.179 --> 00:19:44.169
of their twisted existences upon stars and
planets and people.

00:19:44.169 --> 00:19:47.399
The only answer to this threat?

00:19:47.399 --> 00:19:52.149
These Gods must be destroyed, the slate wiped
clean.

00:19:52.149 --> 00:19:54.749
We could not do this, by no means, no.

00:19:54.749 --> 00:19:57.480
But we cannot allow these things to exist.

00:19:57.480 --> 00:20:01.080
A kingdom cannot have a billion kings.

00:20:01.080 --> 00:20:05.739
We cannot kill the Gods, no, only a God can
kill a God.

00:20:05.739 --> 00:20:10.279
We will bring them here and bind them.

00:20:10.279 --> 00:20:15.869
Bind them until their bloodlust is sated,
until all but one is dead.

00:20:15.869 --> 00:20:21.799
Always a single God remains: the Victor, who
returns to whence they came as the only God

00:20:21.799 --> 00:20:22.799
remaining.”

00:20:22.799 --> 00:20:25.619
And with that, the mystery of Daleport was
solved.

00:20:25.619 --> 00:20:30.269
The Victory Society cult sought to wage war
between the gods of the universe, until one

00:20:30.269 --> 00:20:32.480
victorious being would emerge.

00:20:32.480 --> 00:20:37.000
The town of Daleport was used as a battleground,
with all of the anomalous effects occurring

00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:40.830
as a result of the combat between these terrifyingly
destructive entities.

00:20:40.830 --> 00:20:45.399
And if you’re familiar with the deities
that go toe to toe with the SCP Foundation,

00:20:45.399 --> 00:20:47.869
you know these guys aren’t a joke.

00:20:47.869 --> 00:20:52.889
The Scarlet King and his legions of devilish
followers, the almighty Broken God, and the

00:20:52.889 --> 00:20:57.799
mysterious, benevolent Serpent of the Library
are just some of the powerful religious entities

00:20:57.799 --> 00:21:00.350
the Foundation has researched and cataloged.

00:21:00.350 --> 00:21:04.799
And if what came to Daleport was anywhere
near as powerful as those examples, it’s

00:21:04.799 --> 00:21:08.399
a wonder the rest of the world is still here
after the fact.

00:21:08.399 --> 00:21:12.179
Another piece of surveillance footage, taken
from in front of a church in Daleport’s

00:21:12.179 --> 00:21:16.200
center, depicts these violent deities in combat
with one another.

00:21:16.200 --> 00:21:21.299
Beings of massive size and incomprehensible
shape battling with one another in an ordinary

00:21:21.299 --> 00:21:22.840
suburban town.

00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:27.340
The victory society’s goal may have been
incomprehensible and difficult to understand,

00:21:27.340 --> 00:21:31.720
but the Foundation will never forget what
happened in the town of Daleport, and the

00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:34.980
destruction these impossible entities caused.

00:21:34.980 --> 00:21:37.210
But a single question remains.

00:21:37.210 --> 00:21:42.100
We know that Pangloss transported some survivors
from the scene, but what was the result of

00:21:42.100 --> 00:21:43.100
the battle?

00:21:43.100 --> 00:21:44.100
Why happened?

00:21:44.100 --> 00:21:48.620
The Victory Society mentioned that a single
entity would emerge victorious from the battle,

00:21:48.620 --> 00:21:49.919
but who was it?

00:21:49.919 --> 00:21:55.419
Which god was so terrifying, so powerful,
that it slaughtered the others and crowned

00:21:55.419 --> 00:21:58.710
itself king amongst the anomalous pantheon?

00:21:58.710 --> 00:22:02.690
Perhaps some questions are better left unanswered.

00:22:02.690 --> 00:22:09.250
Now go watch “SCP-001 - The Scarlet King”
and “SCP-2217 - Hammer And Anvil” for

00:22:09.250 --> 00:22:12.039
more terrifyingly destructive deities from
SCP Explained!

